.TH _PRINTF 3 "April 2026" "Holberton School" "Custom Library Functions"

.SH NAME
_printf \- custom printf function

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "main.h"
.PP
.BI "int _printf(const char *" format ", ...);"

.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B _printf()
function produces output according to a format string.
It writes output to stdout.
.PP
The format string is composed of zero or more directives.
Each directive is either an ordinary character or a conversion specifier.
.PP
.B Conversion Specifiers:
.TP
.B %c
Prints a single character.
.TP
.B %s
Prints a string of characters. If the pointer is NULL, prints
.IR (null) .
.TP
.B %%
Prints a literal percent sign.

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of characters printed, excluding the null byte.
Returns \-1 if
.I format
is NULL.

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.B _printf("Hello %s!\\n", "World");
.PP
Output: Hello World!
.PP
.B _printf("Character: %c\\n", 'A');
.PP
Output: Character: A
.PP
.B _printf("Percent: %%\\n");
.PP
Output: Percent: %

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR printf (3),
.BR write (2),
.BR va_start (3)

